# Cloud2Code AWS region scan

Reference material only. Stage notes in `aws-cloud-discovery` own execution.
This document is not a step list.

Keywords: cloud2code, aws, terraform state, brownfield, region scan.

## Goal

Capture one AWS region as Terraform state with Cloud2Code so later stages can
split it, reverse-engineer HCL, and validate. This phase does not produce Azure
or GCP IaC.

## Inputs

- Region to scan (required), for example `us-east-1`.
- Optional type include/exclude filters, tag filters, output directory, and
  discovery name.

Run Cloud2Code with auto-import off so the scan writes local state for reverse
engineering only.

## Host requirements

The runner needs Cloud2Code, AWS CLI, jq, OpenTofu or Terraform, and AWS read
credentials for the region.

## Success

A completed scan leaves a usable state path and a non-zero resource count.

## Blocking

Stop when the region is missing, required CLIs are absent, the scan fails, or
the state file is missing or invalid. Downstream stages must not ask the
operator for the state path; the scan owns creating it.

## Handoff

Downstream only needs the Terraform state path on the runner.
